From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:42:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] freedreno/xenos: CPU maps of tiled resources wait for
 the whole GPU; readback blits at every size

Two order-dependent dEQP problems found by the full run, both not understood:
- CPU readback/upload of small tiled resources: ~10 of 44 texture and
  uniform_api cases pass alone and fail after other cases. Waiting for
  everything queued (flush + fence) before a CPU map fixes most;
  XENOS_MAP_NO_IDLE skips the wait.
- readback by blit: blend_npot_rbo_bgra_depth_component16 at 111x122.
Blit readback fails fewer cases than CPU readback, so it is used at every size
again (XENOS_READ_BLIT_MIN_PIXELS overrides).

